<title>FINLAND: FORECAST - WSOY JAN-APRIL PROFIT SEEN UP.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - WSOY JAN-APRIL PROFIT SEEN UP.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts</p>
<p>covering Finnish equities showed a 48 million markka median</p>
<p>forecast for Finnish publishing and printing house Werner</p>
<p>Soderstrom Osakeyhtio's (WSOY) January-April profit before</p>
<p>extraordinary items and tax.</p>
<p>		     Profit before extras, tax</p>
<p>			   (FIM million)</p>
<p>    Median		  48</p>
<p>    Mean		    51</p>
<p>    Lowest		  47</p>
<p>    Highest		 60</p>
<p>(Forecasts by five analysts).</p>
<p>WSOY's four-month results are due on June 17 at 0830/0530</p>
<p>GMT.</p>
<p>In January-April 1996, WSOY posted a profit before</p>
<p>extraordinaries and tax of 39.1 million markka.</p>
<p>In March, WSOY said it expected profitability and net sales</p>
<p>to improve slightly in 1997 after a sharp profit jump in 1996.</p>
<p>Contributors to the survey were Alfred Berg, Aktia Bank,</p>
<p>Evli Securities, FIM Securities and Merita Securities.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom 358-9-680 50 292, news@reuters.fi</p>
